WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:05.979
Install EchoPath on your Mac, connect your coding agent, and run your
first desktop task.

2
00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:09.489
We'll also cover Linux and macOS virtual machines.

3
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:17.771
Prepare macOS thirteen or later, Python three point twelve, Xcode Command
Line Tools, and a

4
00:00:17.771 --> 00:00:20.367
signed-in Codex or Claude Code CLI.

5
00:00:20.527 --> 00:00:24.177
Complete any installer or sign-in prompts before continuing.

6
00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:32.906
For agent-led installation, give your coding agent the repository link and
ask it to follow

7
00:00:32.906 --> 00:00:34.459
the bundled setup skill.

8
00:00:34.619 --> 00:00:39.579
Request the Mac app, select your backend, and leave optional features off
for now.

9
00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:47.013
For the manual route, download the source or clone the repository.

10
00:00:47.173 --> 00:00:50.406
Keep it in a permanent folder, and open Terminal there.

11
00:00:50.566 --> 00:00:54.182
The app and agent registration will point to that location.

12
00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:00.739
For Codex, run this install command from the source folder.

13
00:01:00.899 --> 00:01:06.298
It creates a private Python environment, connects the model bridge,
registers EchoPath with

14
00:01:06.298 --> 00:01:08.790
Codex, and builds the menu-bar app.

15
00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.890
Using Claude Code instead?

16
00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:15.909
Run this version of the command.

17
00:01:16.069 --> 00:01:18.151
Choose the agent you actually use.

18
00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:20.841
Wait for setup to finish before moving on.

19
00:01:24.247 --> 00:01:27.041
Run doctor, then doctor with the model flag.

20
00:01:27.201 --> 00:01:29.241
The first checks the local tools.

21
00:01:29.401 --> 00:01:32.805
The second sends a small model request and uses quota.

22
00:01:32.965 --> 00:01:36.027
Resolve any reported errors before continuing.

23
00:01:38.913 --> 00:01:41.774
Open EchoPath from your Applications folder.

24
00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:47.210
For this Mac's desktop, grant Accessibility and Screen Recording in
Privacy and Security,

25
00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:49.645
then quit and reopen the app.

26
00:01:49.805 --> 00:01:52.684
Reload your coding agent and run the smoke check.

27
00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.025
A virtual machine is optional.

28
00:01:57.185 --> 00:02:03.587
Open Config, expand the VM connection setup, and choose your route: create
a Linux desktop

29
00:02:03.587 --> 00:02:08.709
with Lima, or connect an existing Linux or macOS guest over SSH.

30
00:02:11.113 --> 00:02:14.526
For a new Linux desktop, install Lima with Homebrew.

31
00:02:14.686 --> 00:02:17.897
In Config, choose Create a Linux VM on this Mac.

32
00:02:18.057 --> 00:02:22.441
Review the CPU, memory and disk settings, then save the connection.

33
00:02:25.347 --> 00:02:27.408
Choose Create VM and connect.

34
00:02:27.568 --> 00:02:33.124
EchoPath downloads Ubuntu, prepares the desktop and browser, and installs
the bridge.

35
00:02:33.284 --> 00:02:35.355
First setup can take several minutes.

36
00:02:35.515 --> 00:02:37.947
Wait for Ready, then open the desktop.

37
00:02:40.347 --> 00:02:45.391
For a macOS VM, start your existing guest and keep its desktop signed in.

38
00:02:45.551 --> 00:02:50.189
Enable Remote Login and install Python with virtual environment support.

39
00:02:50.349 --> 00:02:54.115
Verify trusted key-based SSH access from the host.

40
00:02:57.013 --> 00:03:00.043
Choose Connect an existing VM with SSH.

41
00:03:00.203 --> 00:03:05.459
Enter the guest host or saved alias, save the connection, and test SSH.

42
00:03:05.619 --> 00:03:07.873
Then choose Install bridge and connect.

43
00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:16.899
Inside the macOS guest, grant Accessibility and Screen Recording to the
installed guest

44
00:03:16.899 --> 00:03:17.841
Python runtime.

45
00:03:18.001 --> 00:03:21.126
Restart its bridge service after granting permissions.

46
00:03:21.286 --> 00:03:23.972
Wait for Ready, then choose Open desktop.

47
00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:28.962
JEV is optional.

48
00:03:29.122 --> 00:03:34.391
To use it, save and verify your OpenRouter token, then enable the replay
helper.

49
00:03:34.551 --> 00:03:40.095
During replay recovery, screen text goes to OpenRouter and usage may incur
charges.

50
00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:45.295
In Control Room, enter a small first task.

51
00:03:45.455 --> 00:03:48.976
Choose Virtual machine, allow desktop control, and start.

52
00:03:49.136 --> 00:03:53.017
Task recording is optional and applies to new VM tasks.

53
00:03:55.413 --> 00:03:56.879
Watch the activity.

54
00:03:57.039 --> 00:04:00.494
To take over manually, choose Pause and wait for Paused.

55
00:04:00.654 --> 00:04:02.276
You can resume or stop.

56
00:04:02.436 --> 00:04:06.490
These controls are cooperative and may wait for a current model call.

57
00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:12.039
Successful workflows appear under Stored procedures.

58
00:04:12.199 --> 00:04:16.967
Choose Use as task to copy a replay request, review it, then start when
ready.

59
00:04:17.127 --> 00:04:20.540
The installation and VM guides have the full reference.

60
00:04:23.447 --> 00:04:24.405
You're ready.

61
00:04:24.565 --> 00:04:30.437
EchoPath connects your coding agent to a desktop, and turns successful
work into reusable

62
00:04:30.437 --> 00:04:30.857
knowledge.
